# Ship

Applies when the user says **ship it** (`branching.mdc`). Merging to `main` deploys production.

Start prompt: *"ship it (`ship.mdc`)."*

- **Freeze `dev` pushes** (all sessions) from opening the dev → main PR until it merges. The
  ship PR's head is `dev`, so any push moves it.
- **The ship PR's head commit must not carry the skip-ci marker**, anywhere in its message:
  GitHub reads it from the PR's head commit and skips the whole run, so the ruleset blocks the
  PR with nothing pending. If `dev`'s head is a docs-only commit with the
  marker, push an empty commit whose message doesn't contain it before opening the PR.
- **Dynamite test** of the dev → main diff when this ship is a major release (every `scope`
  covers one; `dynamite-test.mdc` → When it runs), before the merge, with the rival too unless
  `pnpm rival scope` prints `rival: off`. A finding blocks the ship until it is fixed or the user
  waives it.
- Mark ready and merge only on the user's "ship it"; merge with `--match-head-commit` after
  the full suite passes on that head.
- **`gh pr merge` exiting 0 is not a success signal**: it is also 0 for "already merged". Only
  the PR's state reaching `MERGED` is.
- **Pass the full 40-character SHA** to `--match-head-commit`. GitHub rejects an abbreviated one
  inside GraphQL while `gh` still exits 0, so the merge silently doesn't happen.

Related: `wrangler.mdc` → Human checks (compiled at ship time); the **Shipping to production**
section of `.github/pull_request_template.md`.
